# starters/organisation/.cut -- which paths of the full site this starter is
# cut from make up site/.
# One path per line, relative to the full site's root. A directory copies
# recursively. Regenerate from the root of this repository with:
#   scripts/cut-starter.sh <path-to-the-full-site> organisation
#
# The organisation starter: a society publishing its programme in its own
# collective voice. Five nav items (Home, Reading, Circles, Calendar,
# About): a course of reading as a series, local chapters as located pages
# with the places map, a calendar of dated days and gatherings, notices
# listed on the home page, a still photograph as the banner with the
# society's name beneath it, stat tiles, a gallery inside About. Every
# section keeps enough pages for its feature to show.

# moss's own scaffold gitignores, identical between the full site and the
# starter -- not build output, just checked-in convention.
.moss/.gitignore

# site config + gazetteer (places.toml is pruned to referenced places only)
.moss/config.toml
.moss/places.toml

# theme + self-hosted fonts, whole directory
.moss/theme

# the banner photograph and the five other pictures of About's gallery
# (compressed to the 1600px budget)
assets/hall_philosophy_1898.jpg
assets/boat_landing_1898.jpg
assets/cottage_row_1898.jpg
assets/athenaeum_1898.jpg
assets/assembly_hall_1898.jpg
assets/golden_gate_postcard_c1898.jpg

# home (banner, name and mottoes, stat tiles, latest notices) and about
# (gallery, then a metadata list)
Chautauqua Literary and Scientific Circle.md
About.md

# reading: the year's list on the folder page + the first two monthly
# outlines, one real prev/next pair
Course of Reading/Course of Reading.md
Course of Reading/01-october-1884.md
Course of Reading/02-march-1885.md

# circles: six towns in six states, so the places map reads as a country,
# not a cluster
Local Circles/Local Circles.md
Local Circles/Perrysburg.md
Local Circles/Petoskey.md
Local Circles/Lafayette.md
Local Circles/Minneapolis.md
Local Circles/Mobile.md
Local Circles/De Soto.md

# calendar: the Circle's list of its days on the folder page, three
# memorial days, and three Assembly days -- Recognition Day, 1882 is the
# one page with its own map
Calendar/Calendar.md
Calendar/Founders Day.md
Calendar/Shakspere Day.md
Calendar/Addison Day.md
Calendar/Recognition Day, 1882.md
Calendar/Commencement Day, 1884.md
Calendar/Commencement Day, 1885.md

# notices: not in the nav, listed on the home page; four, one per issue
# year plus the homily on regularity
Notices/Notices.md
Notices/1883-01-those-most-in-need.md
Notices/1883-11-degrees-and-diplomas.md
Notices/1885-03-regularity.md
Notices/1885-04-intending-to-receive-diplomas.md
